message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it as below."
title: "Mechanized Analysis of Post-Quantum Key-Update Proposals for CCSDS SDLS-EP"
abstract: >-
  Symbolic (Dolev-Yao) verification, in the Tamarin prover, of two proposed
  post-quantum extensions to the CCSDS Space Data Link Security Extended
  Procedures: the Triple-KEM/Dual-KEM key-update mechanism (Hulsing, Lange &
  Weber, CANS 2025) and E2EQSS (Wildfeuer et al., ESA 3S 2025). Confirms
  Triple-KEM's claimed properties, makes Dual-KEM's security boundary precise,
  and reports a new finding (FB-01): a non-recoverable rekey desynchronization
  under space channel constraints that requires no cryptographic compromise.
  Also shows E2EQSS is hybrid for confidentiality but not for authentication.
